{"name":"Grim Reaper","hex":"#0f1039","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Grim Reaper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A personification of Death as an old man, or a skeleton, carrying a scythe, taking souls to the afterlife."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Grim_Reaper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grim Reaper","blocks":[{"text":"The Grim Reaper is a popular personification of death in Western culture in the form of a hooded skeletal figure wearing a black robe and carrying a scythe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Santa_Muerte_Sculpture_%28part_of_the_clock%29.jpg/330px-Santa_Muerte_Sculpture_%28part_of_the_clock%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grim_Reaper","wikidata":"Q105071318"},{"title":"Grim Reaper (Marvel Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Eric Williams is a character appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. Created by Roy Thomas and John Buscema, the character first appeared in The Avengers #52 May (1968). Eric Williams is the brother of the superhero Simon Williams / Wonder Man. He is a supervillain and necromancer known under the codename Grim Reaper. The character is an adversary of the Avengers. He has also been a member of the Maggia, Lethal Legion, and Legion of the Unliving at various points in his history."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f6/Grimreapermu0.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grim_Reaper_(Marvel_Comics)","wikidata":"Q3109958"},{"title":"Reaper","blocks":[{"text":"A reaper is a farm implement that reaps crops at harvest when they are ripe. Usually the crop involved is a cereal grass, especially wheat. The first documented reaping machines were Gallic reapers that were used in Roman times in what would become modern-day France. The Gallic reaper involved a comb which collected the heads, with an operator knocking the grain into a box for later threshing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Fahr-Getreidem%C3%A4hmaschine_2.jpg/330px-Fahr-Getreidem%C3%A4hmaschine_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reaper","wikidata":"Q1367947"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/DeVauceHours.jpg/500px-DeVauceHours.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/DeVauceHours.jpg/1280px-DeVauceHours.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/DeVauceHours.jpg/500px-DeVauceHours.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of the oldest paintings with conventional \"Grim Reaper\" elements: a skeletal character with a scythe (circa 1460, by Jean Fouquet).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADeVauceHours.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-H0813-0600-035%2C_bei_Oranienburg%2C_Roggenfeld_wird_mit_Sense_gem%C3%A4ht.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-H0813-0600-035%2C_bei_Oranienburg%2C_Roggenfeld_wird_mit_Sense_gem%C3%A4ht.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-H0813-0600-035%2C_bei_Oranienburg%2C_Roggenfeld_wird_mit_Sense_gem%C3%A4ht.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-H0813-0600-035%2C_bei_Oranienburg%2C_Roggenfeld_wird_mit_Sense_gem%C3%A4ht.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A reaper cutting rye in Germany in 1949","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABundesarchiv_Bild_183-H0813-0600-035%2C_bei_Oranienburg%2C_Roggenfeld_wird